<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Double-Bottom-Crypto-Pattern"></span><strong>Double Bottom Crypto Pattern</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3>



<p>A double bottom is a chart pattern that, as can be seen from its name, is the opposite of the double top. It occurs when the asset price tests the lower horizontal level twice but then pulls back and goes up instead. A double bottom usually gives a buy signal as it is a sign that there will likely be an uptrend.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Triple-Top"></span><strong>Triple Top</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3>



<p>The triple top and bottom patterns are very similar to their â€œdoubleâ€ counterparts. The triple top also occurs when the price of an asset tests the upper horizontal line but fails to cross over it â€” but for this pattern, it happens thrice. It is a bearish reversal pattern that signals an upcoming downward trend.</p>



