<p>The failure swing chart pattern happens if the asset price reaches a certain level and then pulls back before reaching that level again. Common failure chart patterns typically involve trend lines, such as breakouts before a fail point, or descending triangles. When these patterns appear on charts, they may indicate that a reversal or pullback is due; however, false signals can occur if the underlying conditions or fundamentals do not support the formation of the pattern.</p>



